course: dictionary
lesson: 11681
title: Tools of the stars
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An astrolabe is an old tool. It is made of brass discs with a pointer, and it helps people measure things in the sky. Before phones and GPS, people used tools like this to find their way.
explain: Read the clues. «The sailor used an astrolabe to find out how high the Sun was above the sea.» Sailors, the Sun and "how high" suggest measuring something in the sky. So an astrolabe must be a tool for measuring.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «The sailor used a measuring tool to find out how high the Sun was above the sea.» It still makes sense, so your guess is a good one. If you are not sure, check a dictionary.
fact: An astrolabe is an old instrument made of brass discs and a pointer.
fact: «An astrolabe» measures how high the Sun or a star is above the horizon.
fact: Sailors and astronomers used an astrolabe to work out the time and where they were on Earth.
fact: Early astronomers and medieval scholars used astrolabes long before GPS.
fact: The horizon is the line where the sky seems to meet the land or the sea.
exercise: «The sailor used an astrolabe to find out how high the Sun was above the sea.» What is an astrolabe? | A type of digital clock | A map of the Moon | A kind of boat | *An old brass instrument for measuring the height of the Sun or a star
exercise: «Long ago, astronomers used an astrolabe to study the stars.» Who would most likely use an astrolabe? | *A scientist who studies the stars | A painter of flowers | A football player | A cook making bread
exercise: «The brass astrolabe shone in the candlelight.» Find and copy one word that tells you what the astrolabe was made of. | astrolabe | shone | candlelight | *brass
test: «Sailors used an astrolabe to work out the time and where they were on Earth.» What could sailors work out with an astrolabe? | Their favourite food | *The time and where they were | The weather next week | How to swim
test: Which best describes an astrolabe? | A huge ship | A modern phone | *An old instrument with brass discs and a pointer | A type of bird
exam: Which sentence uses «astrolabe» correctly? | We astrolabed the soup until it was warm | An astrolabe is a sort of sandwich | The cat drank an astrolabe for breakfast | *The old astrolabe helped the astronomer measure the height of the Sun
